{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"GHSA-j3j5-5m8v-7gvc","published":"2026-06-10T00:31:53Z","modified":"2026-08-12T19:00:08.782445562Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-53673"],"summary":"BuddyPress: Authenticated attackers can access arbitrary private message threads via user_id request parameter","details":"BuddyPress 14.4.0 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability in the messages REST API that allows authenticated attackers to access arbitrary private message threads by supplying a user_id parameter in the request. Attackers can pass another user's identifier to the get_item_permissions_check method, which validates the supplied user_id instead of the logged-in user and is reused by the update and delete handlers, to read, reply to, or delete any user's private messages.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"buddypress/buddypress","ecosystem":"Packagist","purl":"pkg:composer/buddypress/buddypress"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"14.5.0"}]}],"versions":["10.0.0","10.0.0-RC1","10.0.0-beta1","10.0.0-beta2","10.1.0","10.2.0","10.3.0","10.4.0","10.5.0","10.6.0","10.6.1","10.6.2","10.6.3","10.6.4","11.0.0","11.0.0-RC1","11.0.0-beta1","11.0.0-beta2","11.0.0-beta3","11.1.0","11.2.0","11.3.1","11.3.2","11.4.0","11.4.0-beta1","11.4.1","11.4.2","11.4.3","11.4.4","11.5.1","11.5.2","11.6.0","12.0.0","12.0.0-RC1","12.0.0-beta1","12.0.0-beta2","12.0.0-beta3","12.0.0-beta4","12.1.1","12.2.0","12.3.0","12.4.0","12.4.1","12.5.0","12.5.1","12.5.2","12.5.3","12.6.0","12.7.0","14.0.0","14.0.0-RC1","14.0.0-beta1","14.0.0-beta2","14.1.0","14.2.1","14.3.1","14.3.3","14.3.4","14.4.0","2.2-beta1","2.2-beta2","2.2-rc1","2.2-rc2","2.2.0","2.2.1","2.2.2","2.2.2.1","2.2.3","2.2.3.1","2.2.4","2.2.5","2.2.6","2.3.0","2.3.0-beta-2","2.3.0-beta1","2.3.0-rc1","2.3.1","2.3.2","2.3.2.1","2.3.3","2.3.4","2.3.5","2.3.6","2.3.7","2.4.0","2.4.0-beta1","2.4.0-beta2","2.4.0-rc1","2.4.2","2.4.3","2.4.4","2.4.5","2.5.0","2.5.0-beta1","2.5.0-rc1","2.5.1","2.5.2","2.5.3","2.